-- title:
--   Branch residues at a supersingular crossing: kernels and orders
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p \ge 5$ and a package $\mathfrak X : \mathrm{DRModelPackage}\ p$ for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` over $\mathbb Z$ of the full level-$p$ modular function field with respect to `IgusaScheme.jFull p`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, $K$ its fraction field, and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism; write $\mathfrak X_O$ for the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb Z \to O)$, assumed integral, and let $x \in \mathfrak X_O$. Let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ into $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot p)$, pinned by two compatibilities: on germs at $x$ coming from $O$ it is $\iota_K \circ (O \to K)$ followed by the structure map (`hφO`), and on germs coming from the finite chart algebra (the integral closure of $\mathbb Z[j]$ in the level-$p$ field) it is the coefficient embedding `coeffEmb` of the rational $q$-expansion (`hφj`, together with nonemptiness of that chart preimage). Let $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a valuation subring, $k$ an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, $data$ a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence, $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality of the level-$(1,p)$ Hecke $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$, $P$ a place specialisation for these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$; assume $\iota_K$ carries $O$ into $A$, and let $\mathrm{toκ} : O \to k$ be the induced reduction. Let $w$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ 1$ over $k$ lying in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ p\ 1\ k$ (that is, satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace`), and assume the $j$-value pin `hxj`: some $\hat\jmath \in O$ reduces to the value of $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ k\ 1$ at $w$, and some element of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $x$ is sent by $\varphi$ to $\mathrm{jFun}\ 1\ p$ minus the image of $\hat\jmath$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\ k$, with closed images $y_1, y_2$ in $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k).C$, both mapping to $x$ under the respective branch map followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, and assume that under both composites the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k).C$ specialises to $x$. Assume further an orientation condition: some germ $t_F$ at $x$ with $\varphi(t_F) = \mathrm{jQFun}\ 1\ p - (\mathrm{jFun}\ 1\ p)^p$ has image in the maximal ideal of the local ring at the first branch generic point. Finally assume `hconv`: for every germ $s$ at $x$, $\varphi$ of its image in the function field lies in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\ w$, the subring of elements integral for $R.R_1$ and $R.R_2$ and lying in every valuation ring of a place $V$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$. The conclusion states, for every germ $s$ in the stalk at $x$: the first branch residue $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\ w$ of $\varphi(s)$ vanishes exactly when $s$ lies in the preimage, under the specialisation map to the first branch generic point, of that local ring's maximal ideal; likewise for $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\ w$ and the second branch; the order of $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\ w(\varphi(s))$ at $w$ equals the order, at the place of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k)$ attached to the closed point $y_1$, of the function obtained from $s$ by the stalk map of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` and the identification `ffEquiv`; and the order of $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\ w(\varphi(s))$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ p\ k\ 1 \cdot w$ equals the corresponding order at the place attached to $y_2$, computed through $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\ k$.
--
--   This is the dictionary lemma matching the two residue maps of a prolongation tuple at a supersingular crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model with the two branches of the special fibre: it identifies their kernels with the two horizontal height-one primes of the local ring at the crossing and their valuations with the orders along the branches, the second branch being read after the arithmetic Frobenius twist of $w$. It is used in the determination of node coordinates at a crossing and in the identification of crossing widths with $j$-widths.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal.lean

